WHAT WAS CHANGED FROM THE STDLIB SOURCE, found 2026-09-11 while preparing
this repository for publication: the copies vendored here (taken from a
sibling project's own vendored copy, itself apparently patched at some
earlier point) each had their real deprecation-warning call replaced with a
bare `pass`, leaving an unused message-string constant behind as dead code.
Neither Debian's separately-packaged `python3-pyasyncore` nor the
`test.support` copy bundled with this host's Python 3.13 carries an
equivalent live warning to restore from (the former predates the warning
being added at all; the latter calls a different, CPython-internal
`warnings._deprecated` helper that does not exist as public API). Rather
than guess at a "restore," the dead lines were removed outright in both
files -- no functional change, since `pass` did nothing either way, and no
deprecation warning fires now, matching the Debian package's own behavior.
See the git history for the exact diff.
